{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Wait</b> — the meaning of this matter is: occupy yourself all your days and He will exalt you. HaShem — or it is His way, for it is found in our language in the masculine form, and you will see it in the downfall of the wicked, as the righteous before you saw likewise."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:01.825376255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}